00:06:50.870 --> 00:06:53.210
Now, why is it hard?

00:06:53.210 --> 00:06:56.720
Why is it hard to move
from a VM environment

00:06:56.720 --> 00:07:00.080
to GKE specifically?

00:07:00.080 --> 00:07:02.390
Well, when you
have a legacy app,

00:07:02.390 --> 00:07:04.370
to move into a
microservices environment

00:07:04.370 --> 00:07:06.840
you have to rewrite
it in a modern way

00:07:06.840 --> 00:07:10.940
and oftentimes go from a,
obviously, stateful type

00:07:10.940 --> 00:07:12.740
of application to
think about how you're

00:07:12.740 --> 00:07:14.870
going to make it stateless.

00:07:14.870 --> 00:07:18.960
And so that is actually,
really, a difficult thing to do.

00:07:18.960 --> 00:07:23.540
You have to re-build
your application.

00:07:23.540 --> 00:07:26.840
Many of the old applications
don't have that type

00:07:26.840 --> 00:07:30.860
of knowledge of application
logic and just cannot go

00:07:30.860 --> 00:07:32.420
into being stateless.

00:07:32.420 --> 00:07:37.750
So it's something hard and
oftentimes, it's not possible.

00:07:37.750 --> 00:07:41.000
However, your new applications
that you're developing,

00:07:41.000 --> 00:07:44.810
they are modern, they interact,
they're containerized.

00:07:44.810 --> 00:07:46.940
And so then comes the
point of, well, I'd

00:07:46.940 --> 00:07:48.440
like these new
applications that I'm

00:07:48.440 --> 00:07:51.690
deploying to also be able to
interact with the other ones

00:07:51.690 --> 00:07:54.200
and to have a
consistent way to manage

00:07:54.200 --> 00:07:58.970
my infrastructure, my workloads,
by being on containers

00:07:58.970 --> 00:08:01.490
on a container framework.

00:08:01.490 --> 00:08:03.050
And this is why--

00:08:03.050 --> 00:08:05.150
the second point
is, why not just

00:08:05.150 --> 00:08:08.360
