or just move a VM

00:08:08.360 --> 00:08:11.000
to be a VM moving to the cloud?

00:08:11.000 --> 00:08:13.350
You can do that, and we
offer that technology.

00:08:13.350 --> 00:08:14.600
We know how to do it at scale.

00:08:14.600 --> 00:08:17.390
We have customers moving
thousands and thousands of VMs

00:08:17.390 --> 00:08:20.870
in lift and shift,
where the source is a VM

00:08:20.870 --> 00:08:22.518
and the destination is a VM.

00:08:22.518 --> 00:08:24.560
But the new thing that,
here, we're talking about

00:08:24.560 --> 00:08:29.750
is the source is a VM and the
destination is a container.

00:08:29.750 --> 00:08:36.200
And finally, when you're
there, basically it's

00:08:36.200 --> 00:08:40.220
us adapting to your journey,
to your environment.

00:08:40.220 --> 00:08:44.510
And how can we help you
going to a modern framework

00:08:44.510 --> 00:08:46.790
on containers and
at the same time

00:08:46.790 --> 00:08:49.010
enable you to move
these legacy app

00:08:49.010 --> 00:08:52.760
and still keep the lights
on for these apps to run

00:08:52.760 --> 00:08:55.950
